>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Manually reviewed Lewis representation. Compound 3 in the original paper contains four CO ligands, O,O-chelated neutral betaine O₂CC(PPh₃)₂. Input C6–C7 is 1.474 Å (WBO 1.024), Both C7–O distances are about 1.28–1.29 Å. The graph uses a C–C single bond, a carboxylate and ylidic C6⁻, Two P⁺ centres balance the charges; All six phenyl rings are neutral, W is formally zero-valent. Localized 36 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. The atom order and coordinates of all 81 atoms agree between XYZ and SDF. Lengths of 81 nonmetal covalent bonds: 76 within range, 1 outside range and 4 with sparse controls. Examples outside range: 7–48 C-P 1.7500 Å. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

